<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>For me it was in the garden,</l><l>He prayed: “Not my will, but Thine.”</l><l>He had no tears for His own griefs,</l><l>But sweat-drops of blood for mine.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>In pity angels beheld Him,</l><l>And came from the world of light</l><l>To strengthen Him in the sorrows</l><l>He bore for my soul that night.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>He took my sins and my sorrows,</l><l>He made them His very own;</l><l>He bore the burden to Calv’ry,</l><l>And suffered, and died alone.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>When with the ransomed in glory</l><l>His face I at last shall see,</l><l>’Twill be my joy through the ages</l><l>To sing of His love for me.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
